Vendor USB/EFEX stack provenance
================================

Source: Allwinner Tina SDK v1.4.8,
        brandy/brandy-2.0/u-boot-2018/drivers/sunxi_usb/
        gic_v3.c is from the same tree, arch/arm/mach-sunxi/gic_v3.c

License: GPL-2.0-or-later; every file keeps its original Allwinner
header.  The linked image also contains the prebuilt vendor objects
listed in ../../NOTICE, which this licence does not cover.

Copied unchanged: usbc.c usbc_dev.c usbc_dma.c usbc_host.c usbc_phy.c
usb_base_common.c usb_dma_control.c usb_burn.c efex_queue.c buf_queue.c
and their headers, plus gic_v3.c.

Locally modified:
  usb_efex.c           force usb_debug_mode = 0 (the script value read as
                       1); drop query_storage_list and flash_switch, which
                       need the board flash probe we do not carry
  usb_efex.h           drop the flash_switch command struct; DRAM receive
                       buffer size for spinor
  usb_base_platform.c  enable the bulk-endpoint RX interrupt (the vendor
                       path polls once per SOF); the TX-DMA path stays
                       compiled out because the controller's TX FIFO is
                       shared with the status stage

Build: ../Makefile.  The u-boot headers this stack consumes are vendored
under ../include/ub (see the README there); no U-Boot tree is needed.

Other vendored headers: ../include/linux/mtd/mtd.h is the U-Boot MTD
header with a struct kvec forward declaration added; the U-Boot branch
of the original relies on a header we do not carry.

Comments in the modified files above were translated to English.  The
files copied unchanged keep their original Chinese comments.
